  "title": "PHP2Shell: remote code execution in the PHP core",
  "summary": "Two memory-safety flaws in PHP itself, not in a library, that can lead to unauthenticated remote code execution. CVE-2026-109618: out-of-memory handling can interrupt PHP while internal request data is only partially initialized, and request cleanup then treats the invalid data as valid. CVE-2026-109619: request-owned internal state can survive after its memory was freed and be reused by a later request handled by the same worker. Upstream fixed both on 2026-10-21.",
